    "type": "integration",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The first parent of turboderp\u2019s merge still declared ExLlamaV3 0.0.4, while the incoming parent already declared 0.0.5. The merge message identifies the operation as merging `origin/dev` into `dev`; it does not claim a runtime fix.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_450fe329d4454c7aa46f45b8f193f372",
          "call_c23c9e975d704286b028486a00da34d1",
          "call_34a6ba7683cb43e4830f4d75c3c0ae36"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Relative to the first parent, the entire change is the one-line version bump. The same file diff appears in the incoming parent\u2019s version-bump commit, which is signed off by kingbri. The supplied Git tree comparison shows that the merge result matches neither parent\u2019s full tree: it takes the incoming version without replacing the first parent\u2019s other content. For example, the first parent\u2019s blockwise `proxy_err` computation is absent from the incoming parent and is not reverted by the merge.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_450fe329d4454c7aa46f45b8f193f372",
          "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
          "call_ae3c3893f2474af4be51b1bbd91df4ce",
          "call_8a614575d74f45a99bf7e9b120a00695",
          "call_27a52c32fd5047ce8437c65b88dd46b9"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "The merge changes the package base version, the stamp used when creating a new EXL3 quantization configuration, and the tag and name a manually requested wheel release would use. It does not change those consumers\u2019 logic, rewrite existing checkpoints, or trigger a release.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
          "call_769b59f380f54b53a3106c3b240daa86",
          "call_65527f8338e542d282a62883174728db",
          "call_174d7da3b18a4e258bcde5f63f5d4297",
          "call_dcd63bf481dc4ae88b3af87f01321261"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The initial runtime entry records the original 0.0.1 version and distinguishes install-time extension compilation from runtime JIT loading. The incoming parent\u2019s version-bump entry documents the shared version consumers, including the existing-config branch that leaves the version alone and the manual release gate.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_0f385e29093c476db95b2d58143a5353",
          "call_33462b771992444880d342a319c195ed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #33, \u201cError converting model,\u201d reports a Qwen3 conversion file-open failure later logged as \u201cToo many open files,\u201d and separately a GLM4 repeated-output problem. Its concrete overlap is the traceback\u2019s `qtensors_stc.get_tensors` call in `compile_model`, which also writes the version stamp later. The merge changes the stamp, not the failing tensor-read call.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_0c33bcb69d744144ae26b65ecc1fec4f",
          "call_441b5afb4718403e9e0e085e8fc48489",
          "call_65527f8338e542d282a62883174728db",
          "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #49, \u201crunning the QTIP inference code,\u201d overlaps `setup.py` by filename, but its install commands target QTIP\u2019s dependencies and kernels, not this package\u2019s version assignment. Issue #10, \u201cSoooo Cool !!! Thanks a lot for the new version ! I loved the v2,\u201d is general feedback and does not identify 0.0.5.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_734420c288064366adf91f433277dca6",
          "call_ff02a0ed5a4f4210a68bb2ac64b41c7a",
          "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The closed PR #22, \u201cOpenAI compatible API example,\u201d proposes an endpoint for use with chat frontends; its discussion ends by recommending TabbyAPI\u2019s EXL3 branch as a more robust option. Branch and quantization vocabulary provide context, but the endpoint proposal does not overlap the version change.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_baa24bc578814a51ba2abb7221247570",
          "call_b491cb674b134e0e90e4a3cd8936ab70",
          "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The first parent\u2019s quantizer file is the overlap with PR #26, \u201cSuperior 3INST parameters,\u201d and issues #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant,\u201d #42, \u201cconverting to 3.0 bpw causes error; block state has 0 inf values and 34 NaN values,\u201d #52, \u201cError converting moonshotai/Kimi-Dev-72B,\u201d and #53, \u201cCommand A support.\u201d These discuss a multiplier proposal, factorization or non-finite-state failures, and model support respectively. The merge does not edit the quantizer or establish a fix for those reports.",
