    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "build-release",
        "title": "How the merged version reaches packages, checkpoints, and release names",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "`setup.py` executes `exllamav3/version.py` in a separate dictionary and passes `__version__` to setuptools. The CUDA build step still supplies its CUDA and Torch build tag separately. Keeping the assignment syntax unchanged also lets the workflow continue reading the base version as plain text.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
              "call_769b59f380f54b53a3106c3b240daa86",
              "call_174d7da3b18a4e258bcde5f63f5d4297"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "`compile_model` writes `0.0.5` to `config.json` only when it creates the `quantization_config` section. If the input already has that section, it updates `bits` and `head_bits` without replacing or backfilling the version. The companion `quantization_config.json` copies the resulting section and adds tensor-storage metadata.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
              "call_65527f8338e542d282a62883174728db",
              "call_d7fa03e0f22c4510a27f510659b0e78c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The manually dispatched workflow would use `v0.0.5` as the tag and `0.0.5` as the release name. Wheel upload requires a successful version parse and release input `1`; the input defaults to `0`.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
              "call_174d7da3b18a4e258bcde5f63f5d4297",
              "call_dcd63bf481dc4ae88b3af87f01321261"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library check executed the first-parent assignment and the replacement line transcribed from the diff, then applied the workflow regex in Python. The parsed and assigned versions agreed in both cases, yielding `0.0.4` and `0.0.5` and the corresponding `v`-prefixed strings.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c2e16562f5214b4bba0c40a9b86dca35",
              "call_411072b1bf2d48f3b7071903afde3ea0",
              "call_174d7da3b18a4e258bcde5f63f5d4297"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Merges the incoming 0.0.5 version bump into dev while preserving first-parent code. The new value feeds package metadata, newly created EXL3 quantization configs, and conditional wheel-release naming."
  },
